      "EVORAO:isolationConditions": "MDCK cells  were cultured in 25 cm2 tissue culture flask in Eagle&#039;s minimum essential medium in Earle&#039;s balanced salt solution (MEM) with 10% foetal calf serum . When the cells formed a monolayer, usually after 48 h, the medium was removed and the cells were washed three times with saline solution. Each sample was inoculated onto MDCK cells (1 ml) followed by 1 ml of MEM containing 10 μg/ml of trypsin. The inoculum was allowed to adsorb at 37 °C for 45 min in presence of 5% CO2 and then 8 ml of MEM with 1 μg/ml of trypsin was added.",
